  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_resnet_block(x: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list, Ws: list = None) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **ResNet Residual Block** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_resnet_block(x: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list, Ws: list = None) -> list:\n    arr_x = np.array(x, dtype=float)\n    h1 = np.maximum(0, arr_x @ np.array(W1, dtype=float) + np.array(b1, dtype=float))\n    fx = h1 @ np.array(W2, dtype=float) + np.array(b2, dtype=float)\n    shortcut = arr_x @ np.array(Ws, dtype=float) if Ws is not None else arr_x\n    return np.round(np.maximum(0, fx + shortcut), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
